From 90b55eccfa27c04d6034cd7d0a36fae9925033ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:20:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Games] Let a game client ask for fast-forward

A core can ask its frontend to fast-forward through a wait of its own,
such as VICE loading from tape, which otherwise runs at real speed for
minutes. Game API 8.4.0 adds SetFastForwarding(). It does nothing with
an older Kodi, so the minimum stays 8.2.0.

CGameClientFastForward keeps a client's requests. It applies them on the
application thread in the order they were made, only fast-forwards from
normal speed and only returns from the speed it set, so a speed the user
chose is left alone. Until a request is applied, the client reads back
the speed it will get, as it would from RetroArch.
